# Copy to `.env.local` and restart `npm run dev`.
# Use the SAME Aptos fullnode + network as your wallet (Nightly). Include the /v1
# suffix (the app appends /v1 if you forget).

# --- Network (default: testnet — the stable home; devnet wipes weekly) ---
VITE_APTOS_NETWORK=testnet

# Published Sigil module address on the network above (the publisher account).
# Default testnet publisher; override to your own deployment.
VITE_SIGIL_MODULE_ADDRESS=0x568721f98162f03aa564384f15d7ead24b9825a3f35e4c2dba8265bd126ce787

# Optional explicit fullnode (otherwise the TS SDK default for the network is used).
# Testnet:  https://api.testnet.aptoslabs.com/v1
# Devnet:   https://api.devnet.aptoslabs.com/v1
# VITE_APTOS_FULLNODE_URL=https://api.testnet.aptoslabs.com/v1

# --- Gasless (sponsored) transactions ---
# Gas-station endpoint that signs as fee payer so players pay 0 gas. The Arcade
# example serves this at /api/sponsor; point here at a deployed route, or leave
# the default to disable ⚡ Gasless when no station is running.
VITE_SPONSOR_ENDPOINT=/api/sponsor

# Optional: Geomi / Aptos Labs API key for higher Node API rate limits (Authorization: Bearer).
# Create a key at https://geomi.dev — use a Frontend Key for browser apps (VITE_ exposes it to clients).
# VITE_APTOS_API_KEY=

# --- Troubleshooting ---
# "not valid JSON" / "Bad Gateway" / "Per anonymous…": the RPC returned HTML/text
# instead of JSON (wrong URL, outage, or rate limit). Match your wallet's network
# Custom RPC exactly, wait a minute, or add an API key. Wallet "Simulation error"
# HTTP 429 (Geomi compute units): switch the wallet's RPC or raise limits at
# https://geomi.dev/docs/faq
